@page "/pdformmessage"
@using PanoramicData.Blazor.Models

<h1>PDFormMessage</h1>

<p>
	An inline question form for <code>PDChat</code>. One question per tab, answered in any order, one
	submit. Every question is optional, and the whole form can be dismissed - a form that will not let
	a conversation continue until it is filled in is worse than no form.
</p>

<div class="alert alert-info">
	<strong>Try it in the chat:</strong> type <code>form</code> (or <code>question</code>) into the chat
	on this page and the fake chat service will always reply with a form covering every answer kind.
	Answer some, skip some, and submit - the answers come back as an ordinary chat message, so they sit
	in the transcript in order.
</div>

<h2>Answer kinds</h2>

<table class="table table-sm">
	<thead>
		<tr><th>Kind</th><th>Renders as</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
	</thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr>
			<td><code>SingleChoice</code></td>
			<td>Radio buttons</td>
			<td>"Which is your <em>favourite</em>?" Choices are alternatives. Options carry a label and an optional description.</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<td><code>MultipleChoice</code></td>
			<td>Checkboxes</td>
			<td>"Which do you <em>like</em>?" A different question, kept as a separate kind so a renderer cannot show radios where checkboxes were meant.</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<td><code>Scale</code></td>
			<td>Slider with named ends</td>
			<td>1..4, 1..5, 0..1. The end labels travel with the answer, because a bare "3" is meaningless a month later.</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<td><code>Text</code></td>
			<td>Input or textarea</td>
			<td>Optionally pre-filled with a suggested draft to edit. Submitting the suggestion unchanged still counts as answered.</td>
		</tr>
	</tbody>
</table>

<p>
	Either choice kind can offer <strong>Other</strong>, revealing a free-text box. On a multiple-choice
	question "Other" sits <em>alongside</em> the real selections rather than replacing them.
</p>

<h2>Standalone</h2>

<p>The component works outside a chat too. This one reports its outcome below.</p>

<div style="max-width: 620px;">
	<PDFormMessage Form="_form" OnSubmitted="OnSubmittedAsync" OnDismissed="OnDismissedAsync" />
</div>

@if (_outcome is not null)
{
	<h3 class="mt-3">Outcome</h3>
	<pre class="p-2 border rounded">@_outcome</pre>
}
